---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../utils/paths';
---

<Layout title="Home">
	<section class="hero">
		<header class="hero-heading">
			<h1>Minnesota Peatland Carbon Mapping</h1>
			<p class="tagline">Statewide peatland probability, depth, and carbon stock mapping across Minnesota.</p>

			<div class="buttons">
				<a href="https://maps.mnlowlandconifercarbon.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore Maps</a>
				<a href={withBase('database/')}>Explore Database</a>
				<a href="https://mn-lowland-conifers.github.io/03-peatland-carbon-modeling/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read Documentation</a>
			</div>
		</header>

		<figure class="comparison-figure">
			<div class="comparison" data-comparison style="--position: 50%;">
				<img
					class="comparison-image"
					src={withBase('images/hero/satellite.webp')}
					alt="Satellite imagery of a Minnesota peatland landscape"
					width="2000"
					height="1120"
				/>
				<img
					class="comparison-image comparison-overlay"
					src={withBase('images/hero/depth-map.webp')}
					alt="Mapped peat depth for the same Minnesota peatland landscape"
					width="2000"
					height="1119"
				/>
				<span class="panel-label panel-label-left">Mapped peat depth</span>
				<span class="panel-label panel-label-right">Satellite imagery</span>
				<div class="divider" aria-hidden="true">
					<span class="handle">&#8596;</span>
				</div>
				<input
					class="comparison-control"
					type="range"
					min="0"
					max="100"
					value="50"
					aria-label="Compare mapped peat depth with satellite imagery"
				/>
			</div>
			<figcaption>Comparison of the predicted peat depth map (left) against satellite imagery (right)</figcaption>
		</figure>

		<div class="overview">
			<p>
				This website provides access to statewide maps, data, and documentation for the Minnesota
				Lowland Conifer Peatland Carbon project. Maps can be viewed in the MNLCC viewer and include
				peat probability, depth, decomposition, and carbon layers.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<script>
		document.querySelectorAll('[data-comparison]').forEach((el) => {
			if (!(el instanceof HTMLElement)) return;
			const control = el.querySelector('.comparison-control');
			if (!(control instanceof HTMLInputElement)) return;
			const update = () => {
				el.style.setProperty('--position', `${control.value}%`);
			};
			control.addEventListener('input', update);
			update();
		});
	</script>

	<section class="framework-section" aria-labelledby="map-heading">
		<div class="content-container">
			<h2 id="map-heading">MNLCC Layers</h2>
			<p>
				The MNLCC viewer contains a stack of statewide digital soil map products at 10m
				resolution. It includes a peatland probability model that predicts the likelihood of peat
				occurrence, a peat depth model, an organic decomposition model that predicts fibric, hemic,
				and sapric composition in the top meter of peat, and a carbon stock model that estimates
				full-profile carbon stock derived from the depth model. Each model was trained using field
				point observations and a statewide covariate stack of terrain, hydrology, climate, and
				satellite imagery data.
			</p>
			<div class="figure-placeholder"><span>Map framework figure</span></div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="framework-section" aria-labelledby="database-heading">
		<div class="content-container">
			<h2 id="database-heading">Database</h2>
			<p>
				The Database brings together the field observations and training data used to build the
				models. Sources include the Minnesota DNR Peat Inventory, The National Soil Information
				System (NASIS) pedon data, Minnesota Biological Survey relevé data, and 2025 field
				verification data that measured peat depth and collected peat and vegetation samples on
				Minnesota School Trust lands.
			</p>
			<div class="figure-placeholder"><span>Database framework figure</span></div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<style>
		.hero {
			padding: 1.2rem 0 2.5rem;
		}

		.hero-heading {
			text-align: center;
		}

		.hero h1 {
			font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3vw, 1.95rem);
			margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
		}

		.tagline {
			font-style: italic;
			color: #5a5a5a;
			max-width: 760px;
			margin: 0.55rem auto 1.1rem;
		}

		.buttons {
			display: flex;
			justify-content: center;
			flex-wrap: wrap;
			gap: 0.75rem;
			margin-bottom: 0;
		}

		.buttons a {
			display: inline-block;
			background: var(--accent);
			color: #ffffff;
			text-decoration: none;
			border-radius: 4px;
			padding: 0.68rem 1.08rem;
			font-size: 0.95rem;
		}

		.buttons a:hover {
			background: #1a1a1a;
		}

		.comparison-figure {
			margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
		}

		.comparison {
			--position: 50%;
			aspect-ratio: 2000 / 1119;
			background: #e8e8e8;
			border: 1px solid var(--border);
			width: 100%;
			position: relative;
			overflow: hidden;
		}

		.comparison-image {
			object-fit: cover;
			user-select: none;
			pointer-events: none;
			width: 100%;
			height: 100%;
			position: absolute;
			inset: 0;
		}

		.comparison-overlay {
			clip-path: inset(0 calc(100% - var(--position)) 0 0);
		}

		.divider {
			top: 0;
			bottom: 0;
			left: var(--position);
			z-index: 3;
			pointer-events: none;
			background: #ffffff;
			width: 2px;
			position: absolute;
			transform: translate(-1px);
		}

		.handle {
			color: #ffffff;
			background: #282828d1;
			border: 2px solid #ffffff;
			border-radius: 50%;
			display: grid;
			place-items: center;
			width: 32px;
			height: 32px;
			font-size: 1rem;
			line-height: 1;
			position: absolute;
			top: 50%;
			left: 50%;
			transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
		}

		.comparison-control {
			z-index: 4;
			cursor: ew-resize;
			opacity: 0;
			width: 100%;
			height: 100%;
			margin: 0;
			position: absolute;
			inset: 0;
		}

		.panel-label {
			z-index: 2;
			color: #ffffff;
			pointer-events: none;
			background: #191919b8;
			border-radius: 2px;
			padding: 0.28rem 0.5rem;
			font-size: 0.75rem;
			line-height: 1.2;
			position: absolute;
			bottom: 0.65rem;
		}

		.panel-label-left {
			left: 0.65rem;
		}

		.panel-label-right {
			right: 0.65rem;
		}

		figcaption {
			color: #555555;
			text-align: center;
			background: #f1f1f1;
			padding: 0.62rem 1rem;
			font-size: 0.86rem;
			line-height: 1.45;
		}

		.overview {
			border-top: 1px solid #cccccc;
			margin-top: 1.45rem;
			padding-top: 1.25rem;
		}

		.overview p {
			margin: 0;
		}

		.overview ul {
			margin: 1rem 0 1.75rem;
			padding-left: 1.75rem;
		}

		.overview li {
			margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
		}

		.overview li:last-child {
			margin-bottom: 0;
		}

		.overview p + ul {
			margin-top: 1rem;
		}

		@media (width <= 600px) {
			.buttons a {
				text-align: center;
				width: 100%;
				max-width: 280px;
			}

			.panel-label {
				display: none;
			}

			figcaption {
				font-size: 0.8rem;
			}
		}

		.framework-section {
			padding: 0 0 3rem;
		}

		.framework-section h2 {
			margin: 0 0 0.55rem;
			font-size: clamp(1.55rem, 2.5vw, 1.75rem);
		}

		.framework-section p {
			margin: 0;
		}

		.figure-placeholder {
			aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
			color: #666666;
			text-align: center;
			background: linear-gradient(135deg, #f3f3f3 25%, #ededed 25% 50%, #f3f3f3 50% 75%, #ededed 75%) 0 0 / 28px 28px;
			border: 1px dashed #a8a8a8;
			display: grid;
			place-items: center;
			width: 100%;
			font-size: 0.95rem;
			margin: 1rem 0 0;
		}

		.figure-placeholder span {
			background: #ffffffe0;
			border: 1px solid #d0d0d0;
			padding: 0.55rem 0.8rem;
		}
	</style>
</Layout>
